From 9f7fcb8201a0defc25deeb5afbb1bf240faa2c96 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 16:53:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 53/76] ipa: libipa: pdaf: Correct the shading of each pupil
 half

The two halves of the lens pupil vignette differently across the image,
so a region's left and right signals differ in level and slope besides
the displacement being measured. Module calibration measures a gain map
per side that flattens this; Qualcomm's PDAF calibration, which vendor
EEPROMs carry, is a 17x13 grid spanning the image corner to corner.

Add PdafPhase::setShading() to take such grids, one per side, and apply
each block's interpolated gain to the averaged samples before the
high-pass filter.

Signed-off-by: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
